%% alt: Sequence diagram of fitting on the training file and applying to next month's file. The analyst splits the raw listings into training rows and held-out rows, then asks fit to learn parameters from the training rows only: a median rent, a city list, a minimum and a maximum. Fit returns a parameter dictionary. The analyst applies those parameters to the held-out rows and measures the error, then applies the same frozen parameters to next month's file, which contains an unknown city. Apply flags the unknown city instead of inventing a column, and the training rows are never read again.
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant A as Analyst
  participant R as listings_raw.csv
  participant F as fit
  participant P as fitted
  participant Y as apply
  participant N as listings_new.csv
  A->>R: read 503 rows
  A->>A: split: 377 train, 126 held out
  A->>+F: fit(train)
  Note over F: training rows only<br/>held-out rows unseen
  F->>P: median, city list, min, max
  F-->>-A: fitted
  A->>+Y: apply(held out, fitted)
  Y->>P: read parameters
  Y-->>-A: scored rows, log
  A->>A: measure the error once
  A->>+Y: apply(next month, fitted)
  N-->>Y: 85 new rows
  Y->>P: the same parameters
  Note over Y: unknown city<br/>flagged, not invented
  Y-->>-A: same columns, new rows
